{
  "version": 1,
  "loadable": "cal",
  "reference": "util-linux 2.41 cal, built from the kernel.org release tarball (configure --disable-all-programs --enable-cal) because the reference host has no cal; its stdout under LC_ALL=C TZ=UTC is recorded as each contract's expected stdout. No expected value is taken from bash-os output. The runner's reference PATH has no cal, so these are contracts.",
  "coverage": [
    "G69: -w week numbers in util-linux's horizontal layout, US (Sunday) and ISO 8601 (-m) numbering, Julian cells, the 1752 reform, three-month spans and whole years, bundled short options; invalid months and years exit 1.",
    "Guest compatibility pass 5 (G74/G83): pass5-month-names, pass5-y-flag-anywhere, pass5-day-month-year, pass5-operand-diagnostics, pass5-option-order-and-forms."
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "bash-os keeps BSD (ncal -C) output for modes without -w; util-linux's non-week layout differs and is not claimed.",
    "Current-month output depends on the clock and is not checked."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "week-us-month",
      "kind": "contract",
      "purpose": "G69: -w puts the US week number (week 1 holds January 1) before each row of the horizontal layout.",
      "script": "cal -w 1 2021",
      "stdout": "      January 2021     \n   Su Mo Tu We Th Fr Sa\n 1                 1  2\n 2  3  4  5  6  7  8  9\n 3 10 11 12 13 14 15 16\n 4 17 18 19 20 21 22 23\n 5 24 25 26 27 28 29 30\n 6 31                  \n",
      "expected_status": 0,
      "stderr": "empty"
    },
    {
      "id": "week-iso-month",
      "kind": "contract",
      "purpose": "G69: -w with -m numbers weeks by ISO 8601, so 1-3 January 2021 are week 53 of 2020.",
      "script": "cal -w -m 1 2021",
      "stdout": "      January 2021     \n   Mo Tu We Th Fr Sa Su\n53              1  2  3\n 1  4  5  6  7  8  9 10\n 2 11 12 13 14 15 16 17\n 3 18 19 20 21 22 23 24\n 4 25 26 27 28 29 30 31\n                       \n",
